{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LoZ9jbBphbR1qujrFjSuhX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D16 seen vs. D17+ candidates)\n2\t\n3\tUpdated 2026-10-16 after D16 (1095 ids, 123 members; D16 added Ruby). Read with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\n4\tactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\n5\thave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n6\t\n7\tContext that drives the likelihood column:\n8\t- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n9\t  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n10\t  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n11\t  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n12\t  The carried solver (`challenges/day16/scripting-same-same-but-different/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n13\t  `analyse_v3`; ran unchanged D9-D16) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, on one line, peelable by hex/base64/\n14\t  reverse within 3 layers. The real D17+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n15\t  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n16\t  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n17\t  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\") have never been asked -- yet; row 66 prepares for it.\n18\t- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n19\t  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack. D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n20\t  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n21\t  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts): the unix-scripting/web-host track continues (Tcl, Go, Groovy, PS v=3 next?).\n22\t- ~15 drops left (D17-D31). Paths below: `$R=/home/testpwn/huntress-2026`; `source bin/env.sh` puts `bin/` on PATH\n23\t  (pwsh 7.6.6, box-js, js-beautify, webcrack, pycdc/pycdas, 7z, autoit-ripper, ilspycmd). `R/.venv/bin` holds oletools,\n24\t  msoffcrypto-tool, decompyle3/uncompyle6/xdis, pyinstxtractor-ng, LnkParse3, chepy, lxml, and **binary refinery 0.11.1**\n25\t  (AST deobfuscators `ps1` `js` `vba`, batch emulator `bat`, `wshenc`, `xlmdeobf`, `xtone`, `xtchm`, `lnk`, `xtpyi`,\n26\t  `pyc`, `a3x`, `xtnode`, `decompress`, `b64`, `xor`, `rot`...). Usage: `.venv/bin/<unit> < file`.\n27\t\n28\t## 1. Concept table\n29\t\n30\tLegend: INSTALLED = verified with `which`/`.venv/bin` on 2026-10-15; MISSING = not on the box. Never execute a\n31\tfixture's behaviour: run only decoders / AST deobfuscators / emulators on extracted literals.\n32\t\n33\t| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool / approach + exact command | D16+ likelihood |\n34\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n35\t| 1 | PowerShell `.ps1` (v=1 JSON descriptor, `$nativeTypes`) | seen D1 | `$encodedMaterial=[Convert]::FromBase64String(..)`, `function artifact_<hex>`, `[pscustomobject]@{..}` | `base64 -d`; `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.ps1` (INSTALLED, AST deob); `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -c '<decode expr only>'` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n36\t| 2 | JScript WSH `.js` | seen D2 | `ActiveXObject`, `WScript.`, `decode_*/recover_*/inspect_*`, `\"52:90:..\"` | `node $R/hctf/js_sandbox.js f.js`; `box-js --no-kill f.js` (INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/js < f.js` | carried daily |\n37\t| 3 | Batch `.bat/.cmd` + expansion (%/!/call/for)