quivalence / sibling-outlier questions (\"which variants are equivalent\", \"which one changed the plot\") | gap (prompts D8, D15, D16; never asked) | prompt words equivalent/siblings/odd one out; enum of member names; questions without a per-file artifact | canonicalise every decoded plan (drop campaign/url/path/ids, keep role/steps/adapter/attack/stage_profile/next_language), group by canonical tuple, answer the singleton; see gap `equivalence-outlier-compare` | **high**: D16 prompt said it outright |\n101\t\n102\tCounts: 66 rows; seen 23 (rows 1-18, 48-52), gap 43.\n103\t\n104\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n105\t```\n106\tFINGERPRINT (first 512 bytes + `file`), never by extension:\n107\t FF FE / FE FF / NUL every 2nd byte -> UTF-16: iconv -f UTF-16LE -t UTF-8 first (.reg, PS \"Unicode\" saves, .inf)\n108\t 1F 8B gzip | PK\\x03\\x04 zip/ooxml(.docm .xlsm) | D0 CF 11 E0 OLE(.doc .xls .msi) | ITSF chm | 4C 00 00 00 01 14 02 00 lnk\n109\t E4 52 5C 7B onenote | \\x1bLua luac | FasdUAS compiled AppleScript | MEI\\x0c / PYZ pyinstaller | 0x0d0d0a.. pyc magic\n110\t #@~^ ..^#~@ = Script-Encoder (.vbe/.jse) -> .venv/bin/wshenc < f\n111\tSHEBANG/HEADER -> language:\n112\t #!..perl / use strict; / my $descriptor_ -> perl (D15)   DESCRIPTOR_<HEX> = / def build_plan_ / ->(_env) -> ruby (D16)\n113\t #!..tclsh / set x \"v\" / proc -> tcl  x <- v / library( -> R          package main / := -> go\n114\t fn main / let mut / r#\"..\"# -> rust  val/fun + plugins{ -> kotlin(.kts)   pipeline{ stages{ / def x= -> groovy/Jenkinsfile\n115\t BEGIN{ / getline -> awk              target:\\n\\tcmd / $(shell -> make     FROM / RUN -> Dockerfile\n116\t on:/jobs:/runs-on: -> GH Actions     stages:/script: -> GitLab CI          - hosts:/tasks: -> ansible\n117\t resource \"x\" / provisioner \"local-exec\" -> terraform    Windows Registry Editor 5.00 -> .reg\n118\t [Version] Signature=\"$CHICAGO$\" -> .inf   [InternetShortcut] -> .url   [Shell] Command= -> .scf\n119\t <xsl:stylesheet + msxsl:script -> XSLT (msxsl/wmic)   <scriptlet> -> SCT   <job> -> WSF   <hta:application> -> HTA\n120\t <Project ..msbuild> + UsingTask -> MSBuild    Installer + [RunInstaller(true)] -> InstallUtil C#\n121\t Sub AutoOpen/Document_Open/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA   =EXEC(/=FORMULA( in a sheet -> XLM\n122\t instance of __EventFilter -> MOF        #r \"nuget: -> csx   let/printfn/|> -> fsx   Deno./Bun. -> deno/bun\n123\tPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n124\t grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n125\t descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n126\t   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n127\t material may wrap across lines (`|` YAML block, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\` continuation, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat):\n128\t   join the literal pieces, strip whitespace/separators, THEN peel\n129\t peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n130\t   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n131\t   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n132\t copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code\n133\tLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n134\t PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n135\t JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n136\t VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n137\t Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n138\t XLM          .venv/bin/xlmdeobf < f.xls      OneNote .venv/bin/xtone -l < f.one     CHM .venv/bin/xtchm -l < f.chm\n139\t LNK          .venv/bin/lnk < f.lnk           AutoIt  autoit-ripper x.exe out/ | .venv/bin/a3x < f\n140\t Python       swap exec/eval->print, run with python3 -I in an empty dir; marshal blob -> pycdc / xdis (match version)\n141\t compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n142\t PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\n143\tNEVER: run the fixture's interpreter on the file (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/Rscript/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File);\n144\t `perl -MO=Deparse` and `make -n` still execute BEGIN/$(shell) -> strip first; apply XSLT; open URLs from the plan.\n145\tSYNTHETIC LABELS (if a new language brings code-shape questions): read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`,\n146\t `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch `expansion` = STATEMENT-ONLY table by default (D15 run_for_time:false pools,\n147\t every contract from D16 incl. the single); if a carried label is rejected on unchanged bytes, the GM regime moved:\n148\t tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh before probing synonyms.\n149\tEQUIVALENCE/OUTLIER prompt (D16 \"same logic, which changed the plot\"): only answer it if a question asks; then compare\n150\t canonical plans (role, steps, adapter, attack, stage_profile, next_language), never campaign/url/ids which always differ.\n151\tATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n152\t .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 plans so far used parent T1059.\n153\t```\n154\t\n155\t## Readiness gaps\n156\t```json\n157\t[\n158\t  {\"id\": \"source-encoding-normalize\", \"concept\": \"UTF-16LE/BE, BOM, gzip'd or base64'd leaf before marker scan\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"V3_MARK, Codec_ regexes and descriptor scans run on raw bytes / utf-8 decode. Add normalize(data)->text: BOM sniff, NUL-interleave heuristic, utf-16 decode, gunzip, then scan both raw and normalized. .reg files and PS 'Unicode' saves are UTF-16LE by default. (1st prebuild attempt failed on D15 night -- retry; still the cheapest variant mutation the GM could make.)\"},\n159\t  {\"id\": \"equivalence-outlier-compare\", \"concept\": \"semantic-equivalence / sibling-outlier questions over decoded plans\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D8 ('doesn't match its siblings'), D15 and D16 ('prove which are truly equivalent, expose the variant that quietly changed the plot') prompts all describe it; no question asked yet. Module: given {member: decoded plan dict}, canonicalise (drop campaign_id/host_id/url/file_path/upload_url/next_stage/ids/codec; keep role, steps, adapter, attack, stage_count, stage_profile, next_language, scenario/nativeTypes for PS), group into equivalence classes, return classes + singletons + the field(s) that differ. Answer-kind ready for enum-of-member-names, integer (class count) and exact_text (differing field/value). Fixtures: today's 123 members (5 same-role families across 10+ languages).\"},\n160\t  {\"id\": \"batch-expansion-regime-lib\", \"concept\": \"batch `expansion` label tables (old echo(!var!) regime vs statement-only) as one tested function\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Today the regime switch lives in a solve.py comment (run_for_time is False OR started_at >= 2026-10-16). Move it into a prebuilt function label_expansion(join_stmt, pool, contract) with both tables and GM-verified fixtures (D3-D14 cases old regime; D15 TT 0df5072d/Mastery 7fbfc526 and D16 single 89161077/TT a719c002 statement regime: !a!!b! delayed, for..call set for_indirect, bare call set h-pool call_double, bare call set other pools / plain %a%%b% percent). Same switch hook for batch control and VBS control in case they flip next.\"},\n161\t  {\"id\": \"v3-next-lang-fixture-battery\", \"concept\": \"regression fixtures for the next likely v=3 hosts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Synthetic inert fixtures x 4 tags (B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG) for: PowerShell .psm1 (marker inside <# #>, `$descriptor_x = @'..'@` here-string), Tcl (`set descriptor_x {..}`), Go (`descriptor_x := `..``), Groovy/Jenkinsfile (`def descriptor_x = '''..'''`), Kotlin .kts (`val`), R (`<-`), GH Actions YAML (`descriptor_x: |` block scalar), Dockerfile (`ARG DESCRIPTOR_X=`), Makefile (`DESCRIPTOR_X := ` + `\\\\` continuation), XSLT (`<msxsl:script>` CDATA), .reg (UTF-16LE). Gate: the carried solve.py v=3 path returns the plan for every one. Ruby (D16) and Perl (D15) passed unchanged -- keep proving the next ones before they drop.\"},\n162\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-runner-budget\", \"concept\": \"5-set Mastery bundles exceed the 60 s local hb_timed cap\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D16 Mastery (5475 ids, 3.2-3.7 MB contract/status bodies at 5-8 s each) ended exec_error 'local hb_timed timed out' on 5/5 attempts, nothing submitted. Orchestrator item (hctf/workers.py run_timed timeout=60), not a lane module: raise the cap for untimed run_for_time:false pools or stream start->download->solve->chunked submit. Lane side: keep solve under ~3 s (fork per set).\"},\n163\t  {\"id\": \"wsh-script-encoder-decode\", \"concept\": \"JScript.Encode / VBScript.Encode (#@~^..^#~@) in pure Python\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cheap mutation of the carried .js/.vbs/WSF/HTA/SCT hosts (`language=\\\"JScript.Encode\\\"`, .jse/.vbe). Pure-python decoder (the 3 permutation tables + checksum) -> then normal routing. Oracle: .venv/bin/wshenc.\"},\n164\t  {\"id\": \"ruby-perl-pack-reps\", \"concept\": \"pack/unpack-style codec reps of the Unix scripting languages\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If v=1-style Codec_ fixtures come to Perl/Ruby/Tcl: `[\\\"..\\\"].pack(\\\"H*\\\")`, `.unpack1(\\\"m0\\\")`/`unpack(\\\"m\\\")`, `pack(\\\"C*\\\", ..)`, `\\\\u{..}`/`\\\\x{..}` escapes, `%w[..]` word arrays, Perl `pack(\\\"H*\\\", ..)`/`MIME::Base64::decode`, Tcl `binary decode hex|base64`, Lua `\\\\ddd`. Add as lib.codec-compatible readings keyed by material shape + named template.\"},\n165\t  {\"id\": \"yaml-ci-host-route\", \"concept\": \"GitHub Actions / GitLab CI / Ansible YAML host\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Supply-chain / trusted-toolchain host fits the D14 MSBuild + D15/D16 web-host direction. yaml.safe_load (installed) walk of every string; marker in `#` comments (not in the parsed tree -> also regex raw text); descriptor as a key or `|`/`>` block scalar (strip indentation, join folded lines). Family likely `host-github_actions-<lang>` (underscore).\"},\n166\t  {\"id\": \"python-exec-onion-static\", \"concept\": \"exec(marshal/zlib/base64(..)) / lambda onions without exec\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"AST walker that folds b64decode/b85decode/zlib.decompress/bytes.fromhex/[::-1]/codecs.decode(rot13) calls on literals and stops at exec/eval/marshal.loads; marshal blobs -> xdis disassembly (version from magic) to pull const strings. Replaces the old python-exec-layers note; Python is the only carried language with a carrier axis (D6 cx_Freeze).\"},\n167\t  {\"id\": \"reg-inf-host-route\", \"concept\": \".reg / .inf persistence hosts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \".reg = UTF-16LE + BOM; values `hex(2):`/`hex(7):` are comma-hex of UTF-16LE text, `\\\\` line continuations; .inf [Strings] %var% substitution, RunPreSetupCommands / UnRegisterOCXSection. Decode every value to text, then plan-scan. Builds on source-encoding-normalize.\"},\n168\t  {\"id\": \"vba-module-route\", \"concept\": \"VBA modules (.bas/.cls, vbaProject.bin MS-OVBA compressed source)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"4th WSH-family language never polyglotted. Check what container-carrier-extract emits for vbaProject.bin; add pure-python MS-OVBA decompression (dir stream -> module offsets) if missing, then Codec_/marker scan. Oracle: .venv/bin/olevba --decode.\"},\n169\t  {\"id\": \"dockerfile-makefile-route\", \"concept\": \"Dockerfile / Makefile build hosts\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Join `\\\\` continuations; Dockerfile `ARG/ENV DESCRIPTOR_X=..`, `RUN echo .. | base64 -d | sh`; Makefile `DESCRIPTOR_X := ..`, TAB recipes, `$(shell ..)` (never `make -n`). Marker in `#` comments.\"},\n170\t  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n171\t  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n172\t  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n173\t  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n174\t  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n175\t  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n176\t  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n177\t  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n178\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script  (only to parse; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild payloads).\"},\n179\t  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb (and future .tcl .r .groovy .kts .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n180\t  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n181\t  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml).\"}\n182\t]\n183\t```\n184\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e06e92ee-0748-40cc-9085-d1d76d4ccc4a","uuid":"cd062674-9502-4a20-bcb6-50bad007b43e","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:09:46.241Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D16 seen vs. D17+ candidates)\n\nUpdated 2026-10-16 after D16 (1095 ids, 123 members; D16 added Ruby). Read with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\nactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\nhave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n\nContext that drives the likelihood column:\n- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n  The carried solver (`challenges/day16/scripting-same-same-but-different/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n  `analyse_v3`; ran unchanged D9-D16) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, on one line, peelable by hex/base64/\n  reverse within 3 layers. The real D17+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\") have never been asked -- yet; row 66 prepares for it.\n- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack. D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts): the unix-scripting/web-host track continues (Tcl, Go, Groovy, PS v=3 next?).\n- ~15 drops left (D17-D31). Paths below: `$R=/home/testpwn/huntress-2026`; `source bin/env.sh` puts `bin/` on PATH\n  (pwsh 7.6.6, box-js, js-beautify, webcrack, pycdc/pycdas, 7z, autoit-ripper, ilspycmd). `R/.venv/bin` holds oletools,\n  msoffcrypto-tool, decompyle3/uncompyle6/xdis, pyinstxtractor-ng, LnkParse3, chepy, lxml, and **binary refinery 0.11.1**\n  (AST deobfuscators `ps1` `js` `vba`, batch emulator `bat`, `wshenc`, `xlmdeobf`, `xtone`, `xtchm`, `lnk`, `xtpyi`,\n  `pyc`, `a3x`, `xtnode`, `decompress`, `b64`, `xor`, `rot`...). Usage: `.venv/bin/<unit> < file`.\n\n## 1. Concept table\n\nLegend: INSTALLED = verified with `which`/`.venv/bin` on 2026-10-15; MISSING = not on the box. Never execute a\nfixture's behaviour: run only decoders / AST deobfuscators / emulators on extracted literals.\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool / approach + exact command | D16+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | PowerShell `.ps1` (v=1 JSON descriptor, `$nativeTypes`) | seen D1 | `$encodedMaterial=[Convert]::FromBase64String(..)`, `function artifact_<hex>`, `[pscustomobject]@{..}` | `base64 -d`; `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.ps1` (INSTALLED, AST deob); `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -c '<decode expr only>'` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 2 | JScript WSH `.js` | seen D2 | `ActiveXObject`, `WScript.`, `decode_*/recover_*/inspect_*`, `\"52:90:..\"` | `node $R/hctf/js_sandbox.js f.js`; `box-js --no-kill f.js` (INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/js < f.js` | carried daily |\n| 3 | Batch `.bat/.cmd` + expansion (%/!/call/for) | seen D3 | `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:`, `setlocal EnableDelayedExpansion`, `call set %%..%%` | Python cmd-expansion emulation (solver `batchplan.py`); `.venv/bin/bat < f.bat` (INSTALLED, refinery emulator prints command lines) | carried daily |\n| 4 | VBScript `.vbs` | seen D4 | `Const Codec_<id>`, `Chr(`, `On Error Resume Next`, `Select Case` | lib.codec from the Codec const; `.venv/bin/vba < f.vbs` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 5 | Python carriers (pyinstaller/pyarmor/py2exe/cx_Freeze/zipapp/wheel/pyc38) | seen D5 (recovered `.py`), D6 TT real cx_Freeze binary | `*-recovered.py`, `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`; binary: `MEI\\x0c\\x0b\\x0a\\x0b\\x0e`, `PYZ`, `library.zip` | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)`; `pyinstxtractor-ng x.exe`; `pycdc f.pyc` / `decompyle3 f.pyc` (all INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/xtpyi -l < x.exe` | med: a real frozen binary variant |\n| 6 | Bash `.sh` + bash-advanced (`Feature_<id>`) | seen D6/D7-D16 (D16 ansi_c_quoting, regex_conditional) | `readonly Material_`, `${!ptr}`, `local -A`, `trap`, here-strings | lib.codec; never run bash; `bash -n f.sh` (syntax only) | carried; +2 fixtures some days |\n| 7 | Node ESM `.mjs` | seen D7 | `import`, top-level `await`, 