d network evidence; the one-sided indicator\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17 prompt: 'reconcile both into one download graph, and find the indicator that shows up on only one side of the story'. Given decoded plans (url, upload_url, next_stage, host_id) for every member and network_indicators() output, canonicalise both sides (indicator-refang-normalize), return {declared_only, observed_only, both} at host and full-URL level plus the member each declared url came from. Answer kinds: exact_text (the one-sided url/host), enum of member names (which file's fetch never happened), integer (count). Depends on network-evidence-indicators.\"},\n {\"id\":\"download-graph-model\",\"concept\":\"build the cross-file download/handoff graph from decoded plans\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Title base 'download-graph'. Nodes = members, urls, file_paths, next_language/next_stage targets; edges member->url (acquire_remote/http_client), url->file_path (write_file), member->next_language (handoff). Expose graph queries for likely question shapes: ordered_tokens chain (follow next_language/next_stage across files, '>'-joined), integer counts (distinct hosts, edges, stages), enum (member whose url/file_path is unique, root/leaf of the chain). Data already in every v=1/v=2/v=3 plan; no new decoding.\"},\n {\"id\":\"plan-key-passthrough\",\"concept\":\"answer a question on ANY plan key without code change\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"v=3 plans carry keys never asked so far (`verdict=benign|suspicious` since D16; `language`). Generic resolver: answer-id field suffix (longest match, hyphens->underscores) -> plan key, with aliases campaign->campaign_id, file-path->file_path, upload-url->upload_url; ordered_tokens -> '>'-join of comma lists; enum -> verify against accepted_values. Gate: every D8-D17 v=3 id still answers identically; a synthetic `<family>-verdict` / `-language` question answers plan-verbatim.\"},\n {\"id\":\"indicator-refang-normalize\",\"concept\":\"canonical URL/host comparison (defang, case, ports, punycode, underscores)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Network/report evidence is often defanged (hxxp, [.], (.), [:]//, {dot}); hosts like `auto_hotkey-<10hex>.example.invalid` contain underscores that strict URL parsers reject. canon_url(s)/canon_host(s): refang, lowercase scheme+host, IDNA punycode<->unicode, drop default port/fragment/trailing '/', percent-decode unreserved, keep path case. Return the ORIGINAL spelling for answers (exact_text is verbatim), use canon only for matching.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ahk-compiled-exe-extract\",\"concept\":\"compiled AutoHotkey/AutoIt carriers + AHK v1 legacy syntax\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17 AHK and D12 AutoIt shipped source only; the D6 Python precedent (cx_Freeze on a TT) says a compiled carrier can appear on a variant. AHK Ahk2Exe stores the script as PE RCDATA `>AUTOHOTKEY SCRIPT<` / `>AHK WITH ICON<` (plain text, v1.1.34+ optionally compressed) -> pefile (.venv) resource walk; AutoIt a3x -> existing autoit-ripper / .venv/bin/a3x. Also accept AHK v1 descriptor forms: `descriptor_x = text` (unquoted legacy), `descriptor_x := \\\"..\\\"`, continuation sections `(\\\\n..\\\\n)` and `.`-concat. Route the recovered text through the V3_MARK path.\"},\n]\nkeep=[old[i] for i in ['vba-module-route','python-exec-onion-static','dockerfile-makefile-route']]\nkeep[0]['priority']=2; keep[1]['priority']=2; keep[2]['priority']=3\nkeep[0]['detail']+=\" (1st prebuild attempt failed D16 night -- retry.)\"\nkeep[1]['detail']+=\" (1st prebuild attempt failed -- retry.)\"\nkeep[2]['detail']+=\" (1st prebuild attempt failed -- retry.)\"\ntools=[old[i] for i in ['php-cli','lua-unluac','xsltproc-cabextract-yq','tcl-r-interpreters','applescript-scpt','js-deob-extras','ps-deob-modules','xlm-standalone','dotnet-script']]\nnotes=[old[i] for i in ['leaf-ext-list','new-synthetic-label-family','family-name-underscore']]\nnotes[0]['detail']=notes[0]['detail'].replace(\".pl .rb (and\",\".pl .rb .ahk (and\")\nnotes[2]['detail']+=\" D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..).\"\ngaps=new[:4]+[new[4],keep[0],keep[1],new[5]]+[g for g in tools if g['priority']==2]+[keep[2]]+[g for g in tools if g['priority']!=2]+notes\nassert len({g['id'] for g in gaps})==len(gaps)\nbody=json.dumps(gaps,ensure_ascii=False,indent=0).replace('[\\n{','[\\n  {').replace('},\\n{','},\\n  {').replace('}\\n]','}\\n]')\n# one gap per line\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n\"\npre=\"Built by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): \"+\", \".join(built)+\". Resolved: mastery-runner-budget (D17 5-set Mastery 12.7 s).\\n\\n\"\ns=s[:s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\\n\")]+\"## Readiness gaps\\n\"+pre+\"```json\\n\"+body+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\na=s.index(\"```json\\n\")+8; b=s.index(\"```\",a); g=json.loads(s[a:b])\nprint(len(g), sum(1 for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild'), [x['id'] for x in g])\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2435,"cache_read_input_tokens":82016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2435},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e06e92ee-0748-40cc-9085-d1d76d4ccc4a","uuid":"f0fdbe45-eb53-4911-bc57-25a154856770","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:13:29.962Z","request_id":"req_011Cg7sHaTHoHNtx1bM15F6g","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HFivBjDQ9MTXVkAXcrGdUS":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"| standard tool / approach + exact comm